  "drySha": "3af6d457ea5341163b57d4dd3ed12ce4556b16e0",
  "author": "groundnuty <groundnuty@gmail.com>",
  "date": "2026-08-07T00:42:57Z",
  "subject": "fix: ExternalSecrets fail closed on revocation, not open",
  "body": "Independent-review finding (LOW): all three templates/external-secrets.yaml\nrelied on ESO's default target.deletionPolicy. Live-verified against the\npinned External Secrets 2.8.0 CRD on the running kind cluster (kubectl\nexplain externalsecret.spec.target.deletionPolicy) -- the default really\nis Retain, confirming the review's belief rather than assuming it. Retain\nmeans: when a remote secret or property is deleted (credential revoked),\nESO logs a refresh error but leaves the already-materialised Kubernetes\nSecret in place, so workloads keep using the revoked credential\nindefinitely. Initial provisioning already fails loudly; this was\nspecifically the post-sync revocation gap.\n\nSet explicitly to Delete on all three ExternalSecrets (lakekeeper-pg-\nencryption, landing-ro, ingest-env -- the last already got this in the\nprior SiteSonar commit, sharing that file). Genuinely two-sided, chosen\ndeliberately: Delete means a revoked/renamed remote secret deletes the\ntarget Kubernetes Secret too, so the next consumer (a new pod, the next\nCronWorkflow tick) fails loudly with \"secret not found\" instead of\nsilently running with a stale credential -- a pod already running with the\nold value in its environment is unaffected until its next restart either\nway.\n\nAlso removed .spec.target.deletionPolicy from all three\nenvironments/kind/apps/*.yaml Applications' ignoreDifferences list. That\nentry existed because the field was never set in git before (ESO's schema\ndefault always showed up on live but never in the rendered manifest,\ncausing perpetual OutOfSync noise) -- now that it IS set explicitly,\nleaving it in ignoreDifferences would have silently defeated this fix:\nArgoCD would never flag, and selfHeal would never correct, live drift away\nfrom the value git now pins deliberately. .spec.target.creationPolicy\nstays ignored (still legitimately unset).\n"
}
